Self-reflection AI project

I think it went well, sometimes the AI didn’t really understand what it needed to do. I went for something a bit simple so the AI couldn’t really mess that much up. I made a 2D runner game that is endless.

Have I done everything that I wanted?
Yes I think that I’m have everything done that needed to be done in order for the game to work. I’m happy that it works there were some struggles with the AI but eventually it worked out.
What have I learned from this?
When I ask AI for help that I need to be really specific and even need to add some screenshots so the AI knows more what it needs to do. I also learned that sometimes it is better to ask the AI just for an explanation of what I need to do or what it has done.
What didn’t go so well?
Some lessons I didn’t do has much as I could do so I needed to work on it at home for a bit. The AI didn’t really listen some times so I got stuck at a point for a while. Sometimes the AI also did some parts that were already done so I needed to tell it that we already did those thing. 
Could I have done things better?
Yes I could have done somethings better like do some more work in a lesson or be more specific to the AI. If I did more in the lessons I didn’t need to do it at home. I saw when I was more specific to the AI I needed less chats with it so I could work faster and had more things done. 
